        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">A curved treadmill is a specialist tool, not a better treadmill.</strong>
            For sprints, intervals, resisted running and a commercial-grade machine with no
            electronics, it is excellent. For walking with incline, easy steady running, set paces,
            programmes, small rooms and tight budgets, a motorised machine does more for less.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Try one at a gym before buying, check the slat belt, rails, resistance and footprint, and
            measure the route into the room. If you are still weighing the broader question, our
